From 9264deb93eece5ddc7b058caf3fae0561108f0bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 20:09:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 283/283] feat(execution): delegate scalar operands to opcode
 contracts in region plans

Round-4 for u5-region-readonly, based on integration tip 8b5246557.

* Remove the region-level blanket scalar pre-check.  Tensor and scalar
  operands are delegated to the opcode contract: a scalar is expressed as
  shape=[] plus dtype and the frozen contract decides (batch-2 admits the
  where fill and the add/mul scalar sides; exp/reduce report rank_out_of_range
  instead of the old region reason).  Other Core IR value kinds are still
  refused with non_tensor_non_scalar_operand_not_supported, a scalar with a
  non-empty shape with scalar_operand_shape_invalid.
* Express scalar constants faithfully in the plan: request inputs carry
  "kind": "scalar" (missing kind means tensor, mirroring the batch-2
  single-op plan convention), and boundary entry_inputs may be scalar with
  shape [].  Both live inside the region_digest preimage; def-use
  cross-checks the operand kind against its boundary entry, a scalar cannot
  be an operation result, and scalar exits are limited to entry
  pass-throughs.
* No schema bump: this is an additive optional field plus a validation
  relaxation, existing v2 documents keep their meaning and digest, and v1
  stays region_schema_version_legacy.  plan_region still self-validates its
  own document before returning.
* Real Qwen evidence: the three graphs now report unplannable_operations = 0
  (205 scalar-precheck rejections removed); all 4282 registered-op references
  plan, including all 2119 references to the six batch-2 opcodes and the
  where/compare patches.  The merged missing-contract list stays 13 classes
  (reduce_mean 79, concat 69, constant 66, silu 60, neg 30, sub 29,
  sigmoid 24, split 24, softplus 18, div 7, gather 2, identity 2,
  embedding 1).
* Tests: where/add/mul scalar region round-trips, scalar boundary spec,
  scalar kind anchoring, contract-delegation regression; 67 region tests,
  310 with the existing execution suite.

(cherry picked from commit 241067edc2c3b05dd2d7150c71dbad1cf26a902e)
